ssage="UPSTREAM: staging: android: Remove unneeded else following a return  Remove unnecessary else when there is a return statement in the corresponding if block. Coccinelle patch used:  @rule1@ expression e1; @@   if (e1) { ... return ...; } -       else{          ... -            }  @rule2@ expression e2; statement s1; @@   if(e2) { ... return ...; } -       else   s1  BUG=chromium:714307 TEST=boot kevin and pyro  Signed-off-by: Janani Ravichandran &lt;janani.rvchndrn@gmail.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman &lt;gregkh@linuxfoundation.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 5f9001dc4221a3d63e2ad5f6d5aef159c2734704) Signed-off-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I3f252b0c1bff373d80b5f8672bd5871b671b6806 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/516568 Commit-Ready: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="516568" owner_email="dbehr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/68/516568/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I441b6e3fd1264bc5cacc1644777682d34a7de987" commit="b53a744eadbc86861259729cce1c469af97b70fe" commit_message="UPSTREAM: dma-buf: Update docs for SYNC ioctl  Just a bit of wording polish plus mentioning that it can fail and must be restarted.  Requested by Sumit.  v2: Fix them typos (Hans).  Cc: Chris Wilson &lt;chris@chris-wilson.co.uk&gt; Cc: Tiago Vignatti &lt;tiago.vignatti@intel.com&gt; Cc: Stphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Cc: David Herrmann &lt;dh.herrmann@gmail.com&gt; Cc: Sumit Semwal &lt;sumit.semwal@linaro.org&gt; Cc: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@intel.com&gt; CC: linux-media@vger.kernel.org Cc: dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org Cc: linaro-mm-sig@lists.linaro.org Cc: intel-gfx@lists.freedesktop.org Cc: devel@driverdev.osuosl.org Cc: Hans Verkuil &lt;hverkuil@xs4all.nl&gt; Acked-by: Sumit Semwal &lt;sumit.semwal@linaro.org&gt; Acked-by: Hans Verkuil &lt;hans.verkuil@cisco.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@intel.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 87e332d56b2c7dc6733f690c9069f4fe75f21c9d) Signed-off-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I441b6e3fd1264bc5cacc1644777682d34a7de987 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/516569 Commit-Ready: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="516569" owner_email="dbehr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/69/516569/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="If549f07e3223fdbd5d3ee8838f505c7dd9174b38" commit="d0b1b7bd1a22a1fb7b82501f1b0eb6a5628a8ed4" commit_message="UPSTREAM: dma-buf/fence: fix fence_is_later v2  A fence is never later than itself. This caused a bunch of overhead for AMDGPU.  v2: simplify check as suggested by Michel.  BUG=chromium:714307 TEST=boot kevin and pyro  Signed-off-by: Christian Knig &lt;christian.koenig@amd.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Michel Dnzer &lt;michel.daenzer@amd.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Alex Deucher &lt;alexander.deucher@amd.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Gustavo Padovan &lt;gustavo.padovan@collabora.co.uk&gt; Reviewed-by: Maarten Lankhorst &lt;maarten.lankhorst@linux.intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Alex Deucher &lt;alexander.deucher@amd.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Sumit Semwal &lt;sumit.semwal@linaro.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; (cherry picked from commit b47bcb93bbf201e9c5af698945755efeb60c0bc8) Signed-off-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: If549f07e3223fdbd5d3ee8838f505c7dd9174b38 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/516570 Commit-Ready: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="516570" owner_email="dbehr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/70/516570/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I988ea7226235d137f7a512ba706e8047dad0de27" commit="50d9ae4658b829f6d3ff6cd7a681c279a37cb088" commit_message="UPSTREAM: staging/android: refactor SYNC IOCTLs  Change SYNC_IOC_FILE_INFO (former SYNC_IOC_FENCE_INFO) behaviour to avoid future API breaks and optimize buffer allocation.  Now num_fences can be filled by the caller to inform how many fences it wants to retrieve from the kernel. If the num_fences passed is greater than zero info-&gt;sync_fence_info should point to a buffer with enough space to fit all fences.  However if num_fences passed to the kernel is 0, the kernel will reply with number of fences of the sync_file.  Sending first an ioctl with num_fences = 0 can optimize buffer allocation, in a first call with num_fences = 0 userspace will receive the actual number of fences in the num_fences filed.  Then it can allocate a buffer with the correct size on sync_fence_info and call SYNC_IOC_FILE_INFO again, but now with the actual value of num_fences in the sync_file.  info-&gt;sync_fence_info was converted to __u64 pointer to prevent 32bit compatibility issues. And a flags member was added.  An example userspace code for the later would be:   struct sync_file_info *info;  int err, size, num_fences;   info = malloc(sizeof(*info));   info.flags = 0;  err = ioctl(fd, SYNC_IOC_FILE_INFO, info);  num_fences = info-&gt;num_fences;   if (num_fences) {   info.flags = 0;   size = sizeof(struct sync_fence_info) * num_fences;   info-&gt;num_fences = num_fences;   info-&gt;sync_fence_info = (uint64_t) calloc(num_fences,          sizeof(struct sync_fence_info));    err = ioctl(fd, SYNC_IOC_FILE_INFO, info);  }  Finally the IOCTLs numbers were changed to avoid any potential old userspace running the old API to get weird errors. Changing the opcodes will make them fail right away. This is just a precaution, there no upstream users of these interfaces yet and the only user is Android, but we don't expect anyone trying to run android userspace and all it dependencies on top of upstream kernels.  BUG=chromium:714307 TEST=boot kevin and pyro  Signed-off-by: Gustavo Padovan &lt;gustavo.padovan@collabora.co.uk&gt; Reviewed-by: Maarten Lankhorst &lt;maarten.lankhorst@linux.intel.com&gt; Acked-by: Greg Hackmann &lt;ghackmann@google.com&gt; Acked-by: Rob Clark &lt;robdclark@gmail.com&gt; Acked-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman &lt;gregkh@linuxfoundation.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 2d75c88fefb228aedfb135228acb6620db8f0e40) Signed-off-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I988ea7226235d137f7a512ba706e8047dad0de27 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/516571 Commit-Ready: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="516571" owner_email="dbehr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/71/516571/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I88420d49bd5c5e0b0bfeb6cb4380b797f4b6d81a" commit="2228c5fe68ffdce792936a24bec2af645b6bce5c" commit_message="UPSTREAM: staging/android: remove redundant comments on sync_merge_data  struct sync_merge_data already have documentation on top of the struct definition. No need to duplicate it.  BUG=chromium:714307 TEST=boot kevin and pyro  Signed-off-by: Gustavo Padovan &lt;gustavo.padovan@collabora.co.uk&gt; Reviewed-by: Maarten Lankhorst &lt;maarten.lankhorst@linux.intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman &lt;gregkh@linuxfoundation.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit a64d6a68667e61f34b27df294e25da6a45f31ff2) Signed-off-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I88420d49bd5c5e0b0bfeb6cb4380b797f4b6d81a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/516572 Commit-Ready: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="516572" owner_email="dbehr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/72/516572/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ifb81775e3ed9f8f2417788a9a66b0286d53e3c85" commit="d16712ffb20e372d808b7244313d6a0124601f80" commit_message="HACK: usb: quirks: Exclude C920 and C930 from Logitech-wide camera quirk  Logitech cameras are so widely broken that some years ago kernel maintainers decided to just globally slap them with a RESET_RESUME quirk so they don't have to maintain ever-growing lists of individual devices. Unfortunately, some of their new cameras are broken in new and interesting ways: while they can now resume fine (hopefully?), they can fail to reenumerate when you reset them too often.  We cannot remove the global RESET_RESUME quirk without risking to break dozens of old cameras our customers may be using. But the kernel has no facilities to remove a quirk from an individual product ID again if it has already been applied for the whole vendor ID and class. For a real solution we need Logitech to check all their cameras and finally make an exhaustive list of which model needs which quirk. Until they're able to provide that, we can ship this dirty hack to exclude them specifically.  BUG=chromium:706603 TEST=None  Change-Id: Ifb81775e3ed9f8f2417788a9a66b0286d53e3c85 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/521862 Commit-Ready: Min Zhuo &lt;mzhuo@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Min Zhuo &lt;mzhuo@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Min Zhuo &lt;mzhuo@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="521862" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/62/521862/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I221eae30e0cb6d39bbd1a9a745de91d0ea29f9a7" commit="8e321226ac5db96d67394a76234a42f1927a05df" commit_message="Revert &quot;cheets_CTS: Add a new test which test only HW codec in android.media.&quot;  This reverts commit eb44cf9e0bfad19d0ee588dff9a0211ceb7df2ce.  Reason for revert: &lt;INSERT REASONING HERE&gt;  Original change's description: &gt; cheets_CTS: Add a new test which test only HW codec in android.media. &gt;  &gt; BUG=b:32626655 &gt; TEST=Run the test on Cyan &gt;  &gt; Change-Id: I4105583badad3826523d35d8fdea171248b4ddb7 &gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/415691 &gt; Commit-Ready: Owen Lin &lt;owenlin@chromium.org&gt; &gt; Tested-by: Owen Lin &lt;owenlin@chromium.org&gt; &gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; &gt;   BUG=b:32626655  Change-Id: I221eae30e0cb6d39bbd1a9a745de91d0ea29f9a7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/525275 Commit-Ready: Owen Lin &lt;owenlin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Owen Lin &lt;owenlin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja H. F